    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d817">

                <pb facs="1108" n="1094" xml:id="pg1094"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.0443/12–944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-09T17:00:00+07:00">December 9, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 9—10:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1988. Foreign Office states that as commercial law is embodied in existing
                    Chinese civil code, there is not intention to draft separate commercial law at
                    present (ReDeptel 1430, November 3, 10 p.m.).</p>
                <p>Chinese laws [<hi rendition="#italic">News</hi>] Service article may refer to
                    statement of general principles governing postwar economic development (ReEmbs
                    1864, November 19, 9 a.m.; 1974, December 8 and 1975, December 8, 8 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">9</hi>] a.m.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d817-f1"/>) and
                    possibly also to statement on commercial policies (ReEmbs 1865, November 19, 10
                    a.m., and 1978, December 8, 11 a.m. and ReDeptel 1522, November 23, 5 p.m.)</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
